            <ArticleTitle>[Function of time (circadian and daily) of the hematocrit value evaluated in healthy and sick subjects].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>4857-63</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Haematocrit values in function of time were studied in normal subjects and chronic cardiopathoic and bronchopneumopathic patients in clinical steady-state not receiving treatment. No significant changes were noted over the period 8-12 a.m., during the circadian (12hr) cycle, or at 8 a.m. each day for 5 consecutive days in normal subjects. While equally insignificant, variations were more marked in the diseased patients.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
